.TH buffer_putulong0 3
.SH NAME
buffer_putulong0 \- write a zero-padded unsigned decimal integer to a buffer
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <buffer.h>
.B #include <fmt.h>

int \fBbuffer_putulong0\fP(buffer* \fIb\fP, unsigned long \fIl\fP, int \fIpad\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbuffer_putulong0\fP formats the unsigned long integer \fIl\fP as a decimal
string and writes it to the buffer \fIb\fP. If the resulting string is shorter
than \fIpad\fP, the buffer is padded with leading spaces.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or -1 on error (setting \fIerrno\fP).
.SH SEE ALSO
buffer_put(3), fmt_ulong(3), buffer_putlong0(3)